\newlabel{tab:hot-loop}{{1}{6}{Inner-loop micro-benchmarks at $N{=}512$, 1 thread, 64 iters. \texttt {ji}-order is a textbook \emph {wrong} answer: stride-$N$ along the inner loop blows the L1 cache on every column. \texttt {restrict} is essentially free (gcc 11 already infers no-aliasing here. I checked the assembly).\relax }{table.caption.12}{}}
